<title>JAPAN: Rentenbank launches 4.9% yen/dlr samurai--Nomura.</title>
<headline>Rentenbank launches 4.9% yen/dlr samurai--Nomura.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following yen/dollar dual-currency samurai issue was announced by lead-manager Nomura Securities on Wednesday:</p>
<p> BORROWER	  Landwirtschaftliche Rentenbank</p>
<p> AMT		 30 bln yen</p>
<p> COUPON	    4.9 pct</p>
<p> MATURITY	  13 March 2000</p>
<p> ISS PRICE	 par</p>
<p> PAY DATE	  13 March 1997</p>
<p> SUB PERIOD	March 3 to March 11</p>
<p> PAY FREQ	  Semi-annual</p>
<p> LAST RATING     S&amp;P AAA, Moody's Aaa, IBCA AAA</p>
<p> LEAD MANAGER    Nomura Securities</p>
<p> LEAD TRUSTEE    Norinchukin Bank</p>
<p>NOTE: The exchange rate was fixed at $4,113.53/500,000 yen. -- Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-3432-8785</p>
</text>
